{# PM·B — ONE POSITION AT A TIME. THE SHIPPED DIRECTION.

   A rail of every position beside one position's permissions. The SAFEST
   EDITOR there is: you are always demonstrably changing exactly one position,
   and the pane's header says which and how many people it reaches. The cost is
   real — comparing two positions costs two clicks and there is no view of the
   whole.

   B SHIPS SELECTED on the fresh-installation argument rather than the populated
   one: on day one there are no positions, and B is the only direction whose
   empty state is a single control that makes the first one. The grid opens on
   nothing at all.

   THE COUNT IS IN THE HEADER, NOT IN A CONFIRMATION AFTERWARDS. Every box
   ticked here is granted to everybody holding the position at once, and
   unticking one takes it from all of them — which is the point of a position,
   and it should be known before the click rather than after. #}
{% import '@UhifadhiTeam/positions/_bits.html.twig' as pm %}

<div class="c" data-pm="b">
    <span class="tab">One position at a time<span class="src">&middot; the rail and the checklist</span></span>
    <p class="use" style="margin-top:2px">A rail of every position beside one position&rsquo;s permissions. The
    <b>safest editor</b>: you are always demonstrably changing exactly one position, and the pane says which and
    how many people it reaches. You cannot compare two positions without clicking twice.</p>

    {% if positions is empty %}
        {# THE EMPTY STATE THAT MADE B THE SHIPPED ONE: the rail is one control,
           and it is the control that makes the first position. #}
        <div class="pm-first">
            {{ pm.icon_plus() }}
            <div class="ft">
                <h3>There are no positions yet, and the rail is the button that makes the first one.</h3>
                <p>Until one exists, every Staff member on this installation holds nothing at all &mdash; they can
                sign in and reach no page behind it. The two tiers above the matrix are unaffected, which is what
                they are for.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    {% else %}
        <div class="split">
            {# THE RAIL, banded by department — because a bare "Analyst" appearing
               twice in one list is two jobs a reader cannot tell apart. #}
            <div class="dept-rail">
                <span class="lbl">positions &middot; {{ positions|length }} in {{ departments|length }} department{{ departments|length == 1 ? '' : 's' }}</span>
                {% for department, group in groupedPositions %}
                    <div class="railsplit"><span class="lbl">{{ department is empty ? 'No department yet' : department }}</span></div>
                    {% for position in group %}
                        {% set held = holders[position.uuidString]|default(0) %}
                        <a class="rail-item{{ selected and selected.id == position.id ? ' on' : '' }}"
                           href="{{ path('team_positions', {position: position.uuidString}) }}">
                            <i class="dot"></i>
                            <span class="rn">{{ position.name }}</span>
                            <span class="rc">{{ held }}</span>
                            <span class="rh">
                                {%- if held == 0 -%}<span class="pm-held0">nobody yet</span>
                                {%- else -%}{{ held }} holder{{ held == 1 ? '' : 's' }}{% endif %}
                                &middot; {{ position.permissionValues|length }} permission{{ position.permissionValues|length == 1 ? '' : 's' }}
                            </span>
                        </a>
                    {% endfor %}
                {% endfor %}
            </div>

            <div class="panes">
                {% if selected %}
                    {% set held = selected.permissionValues %}
                    {% set reaches = holders[selected.uuidString]|default(0) %}
                    {# RENAME IS A SECOND, SEPARATE WRITE ON THE SAME PANE, and
                       forms do not nest — so it is a sibling of the permissions
                       form and the header's controls join it by `form=`, which
                       is exactly what that attribute is for. Neither form can
                       post the other's fields.

                       DELETE IS NOT DRAWN. The design puts it here beside
                       Rename, and what becomes of the people holding a deleted
                       position is a question nobody has answered — so it waits
                       for that ruling rather than being made by accident. #}
                    <form id="pm-rename-{{ selected.uuidString }}" method="post"
                          action="{{ path('team_position_rename', {uuid: selected.uuidString}) }}">
                        <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrfToken }}">
                    </form>

                    <form class="pane on" method="post" action="{{ path('team_position_permissions', {uuid: selected.uuidString}) }}">
                        <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrfToken }}">

                        <div class="pm-head">
                            <span class="hl">
                                {% if selected.department %}<span class="dtag"><i class="dot"></i>{{ selected.department.name }}</span>{% endif %}
                                <b>{{ selected.name }}</b>
                                <span class="pm-reach">{{ pm.icon_people() }} reaches {{ reaches }} {{ reaches == 1 ? 'person' : 'people' }}</span>
                            </span>
                            <span class="hr">
                                {# The design draws a bare Rename button; the route
                                   needs a name and a static page had nowhere to put
                                   the field that collects one, so the field it
                                   submits is here, carrying the name it is about. #}
                                <input class="fld pm-rename" type="text" name="name" required
                                       value="{{ selected.name }}" aria-label="Rename this position"
                                       form="pm-rename-{{ selected.uuidString }}">
                                <button class="softbtn" type="submit" form="pm-rename-{{ selected.uuidString }}">Rename</button>
                            </span>
                        </div>

                        <p class="use" style="margin:-4px 0 14px">Every box ticked here is granted to
                        <b>{{ reaches == 1 ? 'the one person' : 'all ' ~ reaches ~ ' people' }}</b> holding this
                        position at once, and unticking one takes it from all of them &mdash; which is the point
                        of a position, and the reason the count is in the header rather than in a confirmation
                        afterwards.</p>

                        <div class="pm-list">
                            {# PER-MODULE GROUPS, CLEARLY BOUNDED. One umbrella is
                               ONE bounded group with its rows inside it, carrying
                               its module's own colour on a 3px left edge — so a
                               reader can see where one module's permissions end
                               and the next module's begin at arm's length. #}
                            {% for umbrella, permissions in grouped %}
                                {# THE GROUP IS THE SCOPE, not the heading: the
                                   select-all button is in the heading and the
                                   boxes are its siblings, so only the bounded
                                   group can see both. #}
                                <div class="pm-group {{ permissions[0].isCore ? 'pm-core' : 'pm-mod pm-mod-' ~ permissions[0].source }}"
                                     data-controller="uhifadhi--team-module--permission-group">
                                    {{ pm.umbrella_head(umbrella, permissions, moduleNames, held) }}
                                    {% for permission in permissions %}
                                        {{ pm.row(permission, held) }}
                                    {% endfor %}
                                </div>
                            {% endfor %}

                            {# The modules that are here and have nothing to grant. #}
                            {% for slug in silentModules %}
                                {{ pm.silent_module(slug, moduleNames[slug]|default(slug)) }}
                            {% endfor %}

                            {# And what nothing installed provides any more. #}
                            {{ pm.orphans(orphans|keys, held) }}
                        </div>

                        {# THE SAVE BAR. Two controls of EQUAL SIZE, because
                           discarding a mis-tick and keeping it are equally
                           ordinary things to want, and a page that makes one of
                           them the small grey word is a page with an opinion
                           about which mistake you made.

                           IT IS HONEST ABOUT HAVING CHANGED NOTHING. A bar that
                           always says "unsaved changes" is a bar nobody reads. #}
                        <div class="pm-save clean">
                            <span class="txt">Saved. This position holds <b>{{ held|length }} of the {{ catalogue|length }} permissions</b> the catalogue offers here.</span>
                            <span class="acts">
                                <a class="softbtn" href="{{ path('team_positions', {position: selected.uuidString}) }}">Discard</a>
                                <button class="cta" type="submit">{{ pm.icon_save() }} Save</button>
                            </span>
                        </div>
                    </form>
                {% endif %}
            </div>
        </div>
    {% endif %}
</div>
